  "term": "temporal frequency",
  "definition": "Temporal frequency is the rate at which a visual stimulus changes over time, such as a drifting grating. In this context, it refers to the speed of the stimulus’s time-based modulation that can shape how strongly visual neurons fire or oscillate.",
